{{!-- The first deploy of a turborepo of Workers, as numbered steps: the production URL for the build, the secrets, and each app built and deployed. The first deploy of a Worker takes its secrets from a file, because the Worker does not exist yet and `wrangler secret put` cannot run. --}}
{{#orderedSteps}}
{{#step}}
Give the build the production URL, as a shell variable (it wins over `.env`). Next.js freezes `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` into the bundle:

   ```bash
   export NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://{{> cloudflare/worker-name appName=(deployAppDir)}}.<subdomain>.workers.dev
   ```
{{/step}}
{{#if (deploySecrets)}}
{{#step}}
Give each secret a value in the shell, and keep each value (a password manager): Cloudflare never shows a secret again, and you need some of them later.

   ```bash
{{#each (deploySecrets)}}
{{#if command}}
   export {{name}}=$({{command}})
{{else}}
   export {{name}}=
{{/if}}
{{/each}}
   ```
{{#each (deploySecrets)}}
{{#unless command}}
   `{{name}}` has no generator: put the value its service gave you after `export {{name}}=`. The secrets file is written from it, so a secret left empty is deployed empty.
{{/unless}}
{{/each}}
{{/step}}
{{/if}}
{{#each apps}}
{{#step}}
{{#if (eq stackName "nextjs")}}
Build the `{{appName}}` Worker{{#if (appSecrets)}}, write its secrets to a file (gitignored){{/if}}, deploy it{{#if (appSecrets)}} with the file{{/if}}{{#if (appSecrets)}} and delete the file: the Worker holds the secrets now{{/if}}.
{{else}}
Deploy the `{{appName}}` Worker{{#if (appSecrets)}} with its secrets in a file (gitignored), then delete the file{{/if}}.
{{/if}}

   ```bash
{{#if (appSecrets)}}
   printf '{{#each (appSecretDetails)}}{{name}}=%s\n{{/each}}'{{#each (appSecretDetails)}} "${{#if origin}}NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL{{else}}{{name}}{{/if}}"{{/each}} > {{#if (isMono)}}apps/{{appName}}/{{/if}}.prod.env
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq stackName "nextjs")}}
   {{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{runScript "build:cf"}}{{/inDirectory}}
{{/if}}
{{#if (appSecrets)}}
   {{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{runScript "deploy" "--secrets-file .prod.env"}}{{/inDirectory}}
{{else}}
   {{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}{{runScript "deploy"}}{{/inDirectory}}
{{/if}}
{{#if (appSecrets)}}
   rm {{#if (isMono)}}apps/{{appName}}/{{/if}}.prod.env
{{/if}}
   ```
{{/step}}
{{/each}}
{{#step}}
Check the site, with a retry: routes answer 404 for about a minute after `wrangler deploy`.

   ```bash
   for i in $(seq 1 12); do curl -fsS -o /dev/null "$NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL/" && break; sleep 10; done
   ```
{{/step}}
{{/orderedSteps}}
{{#if (hasAppScript "build:cf")}}

`build:cf` bundles every `.env*` value of the app into the Worker, as a fallback for a secret that was never set. Build where the `.env` of the app holds no real secret (CI, or a checkout without a `.env`). Later deploys are the build and the deploy commands of each app, without the secrets file.
{{/if}}
